 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to licenses to sell liquor at retail for consumption on certain premises",
    "basePrintNo": "S5823",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5823-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §64, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5823\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in\nrelation  to  licenses  to  sell  liquor  at retail for consumption on\ncertain premises\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL: The bill creates an exception to  the\nAlcoholic  Beverage  Control Law, allowing a license to be issued to a\nperson using the permanent catering facilities of a church,  synagogue\nor other place of worship.\n\nSUMMARY  OF  SPECIFIC  PROVISIONS:  Subdivision 7 of section 64 of the\nAlcoholic Beverage Control Law is amended by adding  a  new  paragraph\n(e-4).\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  While the Alcoholic Beverage Control law prohibits the\nsale for on-premises consumption of alcohol at any location within 200\nfeet of a place of worship, this bill  will  allow  the  State  Liquor\nAuthority  to issue a license to a person using the permanent catering\nfacilities of a church, synagogue or other  place  of  worship.  Other\nexceptions  have  been made for certain establishments and do not pose\nproblems for the place of worship.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
